<title>AUSTRIA: ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF MEN'S WORLD CUP GIANT SLALOM WINNER.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF MEN'S WORLD CUP GIANT SLALOM WINNER.</headline>
<dateline>SOELDEN, Austria 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a brief</p>
<p>profile of the winner of a men's World Cup giant slalom on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>Name: Steve Locher</p>
<p>Age: 29</p>
<p>Nationality: Swiss</p>
<p>Previous World Cup wins: 1 giant slalom - Alta Badia (93), 1</p>
<p>super-giant slalom - Val D'Isere (90)</p>
<p>Other feats: Locher captured Switzerland's only Alpine</p>
<p>skiing medal of the 1992 Winter Olympics when he took bronze in</p>
<p>the combination. He has been a regular on the World Cup circuit</p>
<p>since 1990, but has failed to impress.</p>
</text>
